by stof at 2025-06-23T13:09:11Z

@xavierleune having property hooks in the language does not mean that accessing the backing value of a hook is a public API of the class.
What you are suggesting here is exactly equivalent to using ReflectionProperty to read private properties of a class instead of calling a public getter (than might do more that returning the raw value).

Thinking about this again, I'm actually voting -1 on this feature. I'd like to keep the existing behavior of the component that always uses the public API of the class to access things. This makes things a lot easier to reason about (and to document).

