by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-11T17:20:46Z

Sorry for the year of silence on your own proposal.

Taking you up on it: I dropped the PropertyAccess half and kept only the PropertyInfo metadata, which answers @stof's -1. Reporting that a property has hooks is not the same as offering to bypass them, and nothing here can reach a backing value. @OskarStark suggested the same split back in April 2025.

What is left: `hasHook()` on `PropertyReadInfo` and `PropertyWriteInfo`, `isVirtual()` on `PropertyReadInfo`, and the detection in `ReflectionExtractor`. Rebased on 8.2, and the CHANGELOG entry moved from the 7.3 section to 8.2.

Two things worth a reviewer's eye:

* the extractor now checks the real property before `__get`. That is deliberate, since PHP only calls `__get` for inaccessible properties, so a hooked public property was previously reported through `__get`. It does change what `getReadInfo()` returns for a class that has both;
* `VirtualProperties` changed on 8.2 after you wrote the tests. `set => $value` writes the backing store, so `virtualSetHookOnly` and `virtualHook` are no longer virtual, and those two assertions are corrected. I added a `virtualSetOnly` property with an empty set body to keep covering the genuinely virtual case.

PropertyInfo 663 tests, PropertyAccess 493, Serializer 1429, Form 4955, all green.

The hook bypass in PropertyAccess is not part of this any more, so if you want to pursue it, it needs its own discussion with @stof.

